  "seoBody": "<h2>Four steps from site to finished document</h2><h3>1. Capture on site</h3><p>Staff send text, voice notes, photos, and measurements to a workflow number while they are on site, not after they get back to the desk.</p><h3>2. Sort the facts into the right structure</h3><p>Quickler reads the messages, recognises the workflow you configured, and slots the content into the correct report, record, or template structure.</p><h3>3. The engineer stays in charge</h3><p>The responsible person checks the draft, edits anything they want, and signs off. Nothing ships without a human eye.</p><h3>4. Finished report or admin pack</h3><p>Produce the PDF, the document, or the next workflow state. Store the evidence alongside it so the record stands up later.</p><h2>What you actually get</h2><ul><li><strong>WhatsApp input on site.</strong> Staff can send text, voice notes, photos, and measurements from a tool they already use.</li><li><strong>Templates for each workflow.</strong> Each workflow is shaped around the report, record, or admin pack you already produce.</li><li><strong>AI tuned to the job.</strong> The system pulls facts into the right structure instead of behaving like a generic chatbot.</li><li><strong>Human sign-off stays in place.</strong> The accountable person reviews and edits the draft before anything is finalised.</li><li><strong>Files stay with the job.</strong> Photos, voice notes, measurements, and other files stay attached to the record they belong to.</li><li><strong>PDFs and finished records.</strong> Reports and records can be produced in a format that is ready to send, file, or store.</li><li><strong>Simple monthly pricing.</strong> One pound per report. Unlimited users and workflows. No per-engineer licence, no setup fee on standard plans.</li><li><strong>Direct contact with the founder.</strong> While the product is still early, rollout and feedback stay close to the person building it.</li></ul><h2>Where Quickler fits best</h2><h3>Repeated workflows with a stable shape</h3><p>Inspection reports, survey summaries, maintenance visit reports, site investigation records, QA packs, approval flows, and repeated document handling.</p><h3>No stable pattern</h3><p>If every case is materially different, or review and repeated structure are barely part of the job, this is probably not the right first fit.</p><h3>One real workflow, one real example</h3><p>The best enquiries describe one workflow, how often it happens, what gets captured during the job, and what should improve.</p><h2>Compliance workflows Quickler runs over WhatsApp</h2><h3><a href=\"/pages/eicr-from-whatsapp.html\">EICR &mdash; Electrical Installation Condition Report</a></h3><p>EICR capture on WhatsApp with photo evidence. C1, C2 and FI codes flagged on the dashboard the moment they are entered. Formatted EICR PDF for the qualifying electrician to sign off. <a href=\"/pages/eicr-from-whatsapp.html\">Full guide</a>.</p><h3><a href=\"/pages/cp12-gas-safety-whatsapp.html\">CP12 &mdash; Landlord Gas Safety Record</a></h3><p>Appliance-by-appliance checks on WhatsApp with photo of each appliance plate. Formatted CP12 PDF produced for the Gas Safe registered engineer's signature. Stored against the property automatically. <a href=\"/pages/cp12-gas-safety-whatsapp.html\">Full guide</a>.</p><h3><a href=\"/pages/van-safety-check-template.html\">Van safety checks &mdash; DVSA daily walkround</a></h3><p>Drivers receive the walkround on WhatsApp at the start of every shift. Defect photos go straight to the fleet manager. Red, amber and green status per vehicle live on the dashboard. <a href=\"/pages/van-safety-check-template.html\">Full template</a>.</p><h3><a href=\"/pages/structural-site-report-template.html\">Site inspection reports &mdash; structural</a></h3><p>Capture site notes, photos, sketches and measurements on WhatsApp during the visit. Structured draft report ready by the time the engineer is back at the desk. Accountable engineer reviews and signs. <a href=\"/pages/structural-site-report-template.html\">Full template</a>.</p><h2>Simple pricing</h2><p>Quickler is one pound per completed report, with unlimited users and workflows on every plan. See the full <a href=\"/pages/pricing.html\">pricing and monthly bundles</a>, or read why we charge <a href=\"/pages/no-subscription-compliance.html\">per report, not per engineer</a>. Rooted in UK compliance, <a href=\"/pages/global-field-compliance.html\">Quickler works in any country</a> WhatsApp does.</p>",
